// Braille encoding - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# Grade 1 braille for "Hello World!", in Unicode braille patterns
# (U+2800..U+28FF). Eight dots per cell, bits laid out as in the
# braille cell:
#
#   1 4      H = dots 1,1,2,5
#   2 5      e = dot 2
#   3 6      l = dots 1,2,3
#   7 8      o = dots 1,3,5
#   8 7
#   6 3
